From: "wilfred.dore" <wilfred.dore@telecom-paristech.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:47:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] practice: accept the bare 32-hex session_id of Create
 Session v3

Create Session v3 returns a bare 32-hex session_id. practice._run only
accepted devin-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,180}, so a session that Devin had
actually created was rejected and marked uncertain.

- Accept a bare 32-hex ID or the legacy devin- + 32 hex form, nothing else.
- Keep the URL returned by the provider only if it is the
  https://app.devin.ai/sessions/<id> page of this session. Otherwise
  build it from the ID.
- Persist the returned session_id (created_session_id) before any check
  that can fail. An unexpected format then stays visible for manual
  reconciliation, and retry still refuses to create a duplicate session.
- Tests: an actual-shape v3 response (bare ID + URL), URL validation, and
  unexpected IDs that block a second create.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 mvp/practice.py      | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++---
 mvp/test_practice.py | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mvp/practice.py b/mvp/practice.py
index 5fef028..f7d7a7a 100644
--- a/mvp/practice.py
+++ b/mvp/practice.py
@@ -47,6 +47,22 @@ HTML_CSP = ("default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-i
             "base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'")
 
 
+# Create Session v3 returns a bare 32-hex session_id; "devin-" + 32 hex is the legacy form.
+SESSION_ID = re.compile(r'(?:devin-)?([0-9a-f]{32})')
+
+
+def session_url(session_id, returned=None):
+    """The provider's URL only if it is the app.devin.ai page of this session, else one built from the ID."""
+    bare = SESSION_ID.fullmatch(session_id).group(1)
+    if isinstance(returned, str):
+        parsed = urlparse(returned)
+        if (parsed.scheme == 'https' and parsed.hostname == 'app.devin.ai' and parsed.port is None
+                and not parsed.username and not parsed.password and not parsed.query and not parsed.fragment
+                and parsed.path.rstrip('/') in ('/sessions/' + bare, '/sessions/devin-' + bare)):
+            return returned
+    return 'https://app.devin.ai/sessions/' + bare
+
+
 class PracticeError(ValueError):
     """A bounded message authored here, safe to show in the interface."""
 
